//! The `{{Port}}` contract suite, against `Http{{Provider}}` over a stub transport.
//!
//! `docs/roadmap.md` P11's exit criterion is *"every adapter passes its port's contract suite"*. The
//! stub reproduces the provider's exact status/body responses, so the suite checks the adapter's whole
//! branching — request shaping and status→PortError mapping — in the fast gate with no socket.

// The whole file is test scaffolding. `allow-expect-in-tests` in clippy.toml scopes to `#[test]` and
// `#[cfg(test)]`, which does not reach an integration test's module-level helpers, so the stub and the
// runtime it drives are allowed to expect and to take the trait's owned body by value here.
#![allow(
    clippy::expect_used,
    clippy::needless_pass_by_value,
    reason = "test scaffolding: a stub whose own state is corrupt is an unrecoverable test-setup \
              fault, not a contract failure; and the transport method takes its body by owned \
              Option<Vec>, which the stub only needs to read"
)]

